Subject: winebus: request DualShock 4 calibration when a Bluetooth pad starts on macOS.
Author: AnvilMac contributors (Codex-assisted, reviewed by Claude Code), 2026-10-29
Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine dlls/winebus.sys/bus_iohid.c.
Provenance: original change against Wine 11.19, source tarball
73eb0b02dfc0cb0ff4f4d8d36c5786261e9725ac91968ae4d4e4b9a498c4087f.
Not an upstream commit; not submitted upstream.

Over Bluetooth a DualShock 4 sends basic input report 0x01 until it receives
feature request 0x02, then extended report 0x11. Wine's report fixup in
winebus.sys main.c expects the Linux behaviour, where the kernel always makes
that request; on macOS nothing guarantees it, so a pad can stay in basic mode.
Games with a native Sony reader (Rewired in Unruly Heroes) then see no input.

Request feature 0x02 once in IOHID device start, so newly enumerated
reconnects are covered too. The request is made in the backend, not through
IOCTL_HID_GET_FEATURE, so Wine's conversion back to report 0x01 stays on for
generic HID/DirectInput readers. Failure only logs a warning. Limited to
054c:09cc over Bluetooth (the model tested); no USB or DualSense change.

Tested 2026-10-29 with a local build of this code on 11.19-10 and the owner's
pad: after a fresh connect the pad sent basic reports until the request, then
extended ones; Unruly Heroes controls worked at startup and after an in-game
disconnect/reconnect (request repeated); Shank kept working on converted reports.

Protocol reference (consulted 2026-10-29): SDL_hidapi_ps4.c,
HIDAPI_DriverPS4_LoadOfficialCalibrationData. No SDL code copied.
https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/main/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_ps4.c
---
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_iohid.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_iohid.c
@@ -136,6 +136,7 @@
     struct unix_device unix_device;
     IOHIDDeviceRef device;
     uint8_t *buffer;
+    BOOL dualshock4_bluetooth;
 };
 
 static inline struct iohid_device *impl_from_unix_device(struct unix_device *iface)
@@ -180,6 +181,23 @@
 {
 }
 
+/* Requesting calibration report 0x02 enables extended Bluetooth input. Keep
+ * winebus's report fixups enabled so generic HID/DirectInput readers still get
+ * report 0x01; a native Sony reader can opt into extended reports as before.
+ */
+static void iohid_device_init_dualshock4(struct iohid_device *impl)
+{
+    uint8_t report[64] = {0x02};
+    CFIndex length = sizeof(report);
+    IOReturn ret;
+
+    ret = IOHIDDeviceGetReport(impl->device, kIOHIDReportTypeFeature, report[0], report, &length);
+    if (ret != kIOReturnSuccess)
+        WARN("DualShock4 Bluetooth calibration request failed: %#x\n", (unsigned int)ret);
+    else
+        TRACE("DualShock4 Bluetooth calibration requested, length %ld\n", (long)length);
+}
+
 static NTSTATUS iohid_device_start(struct unix_device *iface)
 {
     DWORD length;
@@ -191,6 +209,7 @@
     impl->buffer = malloc(length);
 
     IOHIDDeviceRegisterInputReportCallback(impl->device, impl->buffer, length, handle_IOHIDDeviceIOHIDReportCallback, iface);
+    if (impl->dualshock4_bluetooth) iohid_device_init_dualshock4(impl);
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
@@ -448,6 +467,8 @@
     list_add_tail(&device_list, &impl->unix_device.entry);
     impl->device = IOHIDDevice;
     impl->buffer = NULL;
+    /* Limited to the Bluetooth model verified with hardware. */
+    impl->dualshock4_bluetooth = desc.bus_type == BUS_TYPE_BLUETOOTH && desc.vid == 0x054c && desc.pid == 0x09cc;
 
     bus_event_queue_device_created(&event_queue, &impl->unix_device, &desc);
 }
